# Created by .ignore support plugin (hsz.mobi)
### Go template
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Editors
.idea/*

**/sponge_log.log

testing/kokoro/test-env.sh
.envrc

# The deploy folder is ignored by default -- it is where environment-specific
# and generated files land. The manifests below are the exception: they define
# how this is deployed and monitored, and keeping them out of version control
# is what left the Prometheus scrape job and the headless Service living only
# on the clusters. Listed one directory at a time rather than lifting the
# ignore, so a credential file dropped in deploy/ is still ignored.
#
# "deploy/*" rather than "deploy/": git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so a negation inside one has no effect.
deploy/*
!deploy/README.md
!deploy/kubernetes/
!deploy/prometheus/

# Ignore config file
env.json
config_*.yaml
config.yaml
config.json
.DS_Store
.goreleaser.yaml
dist/

/sync
cloudbuild.yaml
docker-compose-demo.yml
# The control database. It used to be committed, which shipped one admin
# password — and the connection strings of whoever committed it last — to
# every clone. The program creates the file and its schema on first run.
sync.db
sync.db-wal
sync.db-shm
# The SQLite file belongs at the repository root only; a copy anywhere else
# means the SYNC_DB_PATH fallback in internal/platform/db/init.go resolved to
# the wrong directory.
*/sync.db
*/*/sync.db
*/*/*/sync.db
CLAUDE.md
.cursorrules
.cursor
decrypt
decode_bson.js

# Ignore internal docs
docs/
# Binaries produced by "go build ./scripts/..."
/mint
